description: dccpr means Document, Commit, Check, Push, PR
alwaysApply: true
---

# dccpr

When the user says **`dccpr`**, do all five steps. When they say **`dcp`**, stop after Push (no PR).

1. **Document** — refresh `NEXT.md` with current state, decisions made, blockers,
   and next steps. Update `STATUS.md` only if the long-form record changed.
   Do **not** commit `NEXT.md` / `STATUS.md` / other gitignored local notes.
2. **Commit** — stage only task files; create small logical commit(s) per repo
   commit protocol. Never secrets, never force-push, never amend unless John asks.
3. **Check** — run the smoke that matches the change (at minimum: `git status`,
   and for runtime work: watchdog/socket/`sbbrain`). Fix must-fix failures
   before claiming done.
4. **Push** — `git push` to the tracked remote branch.
5. **PR** — open a PR if none exists for this unit, or update the existing one.
   Title with `[category]` per CONTRIBUTING. Note Bugbot/CI; do not treat green
   CI alone as “reviewed.”

Do not skip steps unless the user explicitly narrows the request
(e.g. “just document”, “commit only”).
